module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeVeryAmpleTwist.CanonicalSymSurjective

/-!
# The relative `Proj` of an algebra generated in degree one is projective

Let `S` be a scheme and `𝒜` a quasi-coherent graded `𝒪_S`-algebra generated by `𝒜_1` over `𝒜_0`,
with `𝒜_1` of finite type over `𝒪_S`, and set `X = Proj_S(𝒜)`. Stacks Example 07ZS says that
`X ⟶ S` is projective, in the sense of Tag 01W8, because the morphism attached to the canonical
graded-algebra map `Sym(𝒜_1) ⟶ 𝒜` is a closed immersion `X ⟶ 𝐏(𝒜_1)` over `S`, by Tag 07ZK.
(The source writes `Sym_{𝒪_X}`; the symmetric algebra is that of the `𝒪_S`-module `𝒜_1`.)

This file states that, with the closed immersion in the statement: the projection
`Proj_S(𝒜) ⟶ S` is projective, the morphism
`Stacks.Tag01VMRelativeVeryAmple.canonicalSymProjHom 𝒜 _ : Proj_S(𝒜) ⟶ 𝐏(𝒜_1)` attached to
`Stacks.Tag01VMRelativeVeryAmple.canonicalSymHom 𝒜 : Sym(𝒜_1) ⟶ 𝒜` is a closed immersion, and it
is a morphism over `S`. Its target is the projective bundle
`Stacks.SymGraded.schemeProjectiveBundle 𝒜_1 _` that `AlgebraicGeometry.IsProjective` quantifies
over.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.isProjective_relativeProj_toBase_and_isClosedImmersion`: **Stacks Example
  07ZS.**

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07ZS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07ZS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07ZK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07ZK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01W8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01W8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B3U](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B3U)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProj
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjBridge

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- **Stacks Project, Example 07ZS.** Let `S` be a scheme and `𝒜` a quasi-coherent graded
`𝒪_S`-algebra generated by `𝒜_1` over `𝒜_0`, with `𝒜_1` of finite type over `𝒪_S`, and let
`X = Proj_S(𝒜)`. Then `X ⟶ S` is projective (Tag 01W8), and the morphism
`X ⟶ 𝐏(𝒜_1) = Proj_S(Sym(𝒜_1))` associated to the canonical graded `𝒪_S`-algebra map
`Sym(𝒜_1) ⟶ 𝒜` is a closed immersion over `S`.

The three conjuncts are, in order: projectivity of the projection of `Proj_S(𝒜)`; the closed
immersion `Stacks.Tag01VMRelativeVeryAmple.canonicalSymProjHom`, which is Tag 07ZK (2) for the
canonical map; and its compatibility with the projections to `S`. The first is Tag 0B3U,
`AlgebraicGeometry.isProjective_relativeProj_toBase`, which is proved from the other two. -/
@[stacks 07ZS]
theorem isProjective_relativeProj_toBase_and_isClosedImmersion {S : Scheme.{u}}
    (A : SheafGradedAlgebra.{u} S)
    (hgen : Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjRepresentsF1.IsGeneratedInDegreeOne A)
    (hfin : (A.piece 1).IsFiniteType) :
    IsProjective (relativeProj A).toBase ∧
      IsClosedImmersion (Stacks.Tag01VMRelativeVeryAmple.canonicalSymProjHom A hgen) ∧
      Stacks.Tag01VMRelativeVeryAmple.canonicalSymProjHom A hgen ≫
          (Stacks.SymGraded.schemeProjectiveBundle (A.piece 1)
            (Stacks.SymGraded.isQuasicoherentPieces_of_isQuasicoherent (A.piece 1))).toBase =
        (relativeProj A).toBase :=
  ⟨isProjective_relativeProj_toBase A hgen hfin,
    Stacks.Tag01VMRelativeVeryAmple.isClosedImmersion_canonicalSymProjHom A hgen,
    Stacks.Tag01VMRelativeVeryAmple.canonicalSymProjHom_comp_toBase A hgen⟩

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
